{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria","id":996449,"title":"Weird Experiment: Changeling Meets Requiem, The Admonitoria","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T22:03:44-07:00","id":996449,"title":"Weird Experiment: Changeling Meets Requiem, The Admonitoria","content":"So, I wanted to send a thank you letter to a friend and fan, Peter Mars. He did me a solid, and I wanted to say thanks. But, then I realized it'd be more fun if instead of just writing some thank you, I did some experimental game content and made it sort of a public, community thank you. So we briefly talked, and a little about the intersection of Vampire and Changeling. I wanted to play around with the idea some. So, here's a little experiment. I had to keep the word count low lest I spend forever working on it. But, it's a basically playable experiment. Basically, the idea is, &quot;What if the embrace is a changeling's method of escape? Is that her Seeming?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it's pretty barebones. People are welcome to and encouraged to build on it if they want. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyodWhkbDNWSzdvRlU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 11-01-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:22:12-07:00","id":996454,"title":"","content":"I love this kind of experimental strangeness. It's the kind of thing that really pushes that 'no neat little boxes' element of the Chronicles of Darkness. Thanks for sharing it with us, David!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:39:38-07:00","id":996459,"title":"","content":"My freehold has a court where a third of the members were Vampires so this will fit in brilliantly. I especially like how you blended them without it just seeming like Vampire with Changeling on top or Changeling with Vampire on top, instead seeming like a broken mix of the two (their mask seems especially cruel). The fact that the beast is the one actually making bargains will be rather interesting to explore in my games. <br /> <br /> One question though. When a trigger occurs, what happens on a success?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:59:51-07:00","id":996464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996459#post996459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question though. When a trigger occurs, what happens on a success?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gosh. I forgot that, didn't I? <br /> <br /> Success lets you keep your Balance, but you gain a Condition you have to cope with. Just a little thing like Guilty or Shaken. <br /> <br /> Exceptional Success gives you a positive Condition and I'd say probably gives you a dot of Balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T23:11:39-07:00","id":996467,"title":"","content":"This is quite cool.<br /> <br /> No comment on mechanics yet, but I love the fiction behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T23:37:23-07:00","id":996469,"title":"","content":"Oh man. This is awesome. <i>This</i> is how you do template mixing! This gives me so many ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:26:23-07:00","id":996480,"title":"","content":"Wow. You've managed to take something that instills the most profound knee-jerk kill on sight response possible (&quot;I'm a fairy <i>and</i> a vampire!&quot; either screams of really, really wanting attention or being a heinous power-gamer) and make it instead a valid and rich concept that adds to both games it draws from. Would it be alright to attempt similar mergers between other gamelines, or would that be stepping on your toes too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:26:28-07:00","id":996481,"title":"","content":"I see that Advanced and Legendary Merits from B:tP are in (I suppose Epic Merits are now called Legendary Merits?) Those give me so much ideas for Bloodline customization.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it's mien, not mein, right? Don't want to sound edgy and I used to be sure that it's supposed to be mien and will be corrected later, but I keep seeing those two mixed up and now I'm not sure what's the intended vocab...<br /> <br /> EDIT: And dang, I realize that this also works as a fantastic translation of the Kiasyd from VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 11-01-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:40:46-07:00","id":996486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996481#post996481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that Advanced and Legendary Merits from B:tP are in (I suppose Epic Merits are now called Legendary Merits?) Those give me so much ideas for Bloodline customization.<br /> <br /> Oh, and it's mien, not mein, right? Don't want to sound edgy and I used to be sure that it's supposed to be mien and will be corrected later, but I keep seeing those two mixed up and now I'm not sure what's the intended vocab...<br /> <br /> EDIT: And dang, I realize that this also works as a fantastic translation of the Kiasyd from VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm calling them Legendary there because it sounded better at the time, and it's a first draft. (Realistically, I'd probably make it Epic in final draft form if I were doing that.) <br /> <br /> And yeah, the spelling should be Mien. <br /> <br /> But Kiasyd were definitely on my mind when I was thinking of this. They're not a perfect port, but that'd be weird if they were. It's definitely a spiritual successor to the idea. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996480#post996480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. You've managed to take something that instills the most profound knee-jerk kill on sight response possible (&quot;I'm a fairy <i>and</i> a vampire!&quot; either screams of really, really wanting attention or being a heinous power-gamer) and make it instead a valid and rich concept that adds to both games it draws from. Would it be alright to attempt similar mergers between other gamelines, or would that be stepping on your toes too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please. Go right ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:42:18-07:00","id":996487,"title":"","content":"So cool. And I'm always happy to see more Advanced Merits!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:50:09-07:00","id":996489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996480#post996480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.Would it be alright to attempt similar mergers between other gamelines, or would that be stepping on your toes too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much what I was attempting to express with &quot;this gives me so many ideas.&quot; Thank you for asking, and thank you, David, for approving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996481#post996481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And dang, I realize that this also works as a fantastic translation of the Kiasyd from VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about Kiasyd when reading this too. This is like... A much cooler take on a similar concept, and would almost certainly end up going into masquiem if I ever ran it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T01:17:58-07:00","id":996491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996489#post996489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much what I was attempting to express with &quot;this gives me so many ideas.&quot; Thank you for asking, and thank you, David, for approving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly trying to think of how to work some weirdness involving Demon soul pacts into another line, or what a Kindred Sadikh looks like.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T01:19:08-07:00","id":996492,"title":"","content":"You opened a flood gate here David. Mixing two templates has been a no no for chronicles of darkness.<br /> And I love you all the more for it. <br /> This is truly fantastic, so many possibility are now available.<br /> Thanks for being awesome David A Hill Jr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T02:19:46-07:00","id":996502,"title":"","content":"How would the discipline spread look at creation, given they have no in-clans? Would it be that they can spend 2 dots in the basic disciplines (animalism, obfuscate, celerity, vigor and resilience) and a third as they like, or all 3 have to be spent in those, or no starting disciplines at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T02:59:51-07:00","id":996511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996502#post996502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the discipline spread look at creation, given they have no in-clans? Would it be that they can spend 2 dots in the basic disciplines (animalism, obfuscate, celerity, vigor and resilience) and a third as they like, or all 3 have to be spent in those, or no starting disciplines at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>3 of any from the list would be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T03:04:36-07:00","id":996512,"title":"","content":"I was working on a 2e Kaisyd a while back. That was more of a low-change thing akin to the Dead Wolves from 1e (which I also wanted to remake, though that's much simpler). Faetouched or Enscorcelled mortals or Fetches or even Changelings that were Embraced, depending on however the group wanted to use them. I like crossover Z-splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T03:12:03-07:00","id":996515,"title":"","content":"This is amazing. As far as I know, Chronicles of Darkness never allowed mixing splats due to the experiences with Samuel Haight and overpowered characters.<br /> I feel like your proposal is a wonderful way of providing meaningful mixing: not overpowered, but narratively intriguing. Thank you!<br /> <br /> And now all I can think of is how a Kindred-Uratha would suffer for being a death / blood spirits aligned sucker having to deal with both Frenzy and Kuruth at the same time, always on the brink of lashing out, hunting down. Basically a Werewolf who experienced his First Change right as he is being Embraced, he is a spiritual creature tainted with undeath, less Hunter, more Parasite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T04:39:23-07:00","id":996527,"title":"","content":"I didn't expect to ever see something quite like this in the Chronicles of Darkness, and I am all the more astounded for how smoothly it's presented. It's such an unusual and deeply woven mixture, but the final substance ends up being so interesting. I think it really works.<br /> <br /> The Admonitoria really bring out the strange and ambiguous edges of the setting, and they're lovely inspiration for similar classification-confounding things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-01-2016, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T05:01:12-07:00","id":996532,"title":"","content":"&quot;References to Wyrd become Blood Potency. References to Wyrd become Balance.&quot; I presume that second Wyrd is supposed to be Clarity?<br /> <br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> <br /> Shouldn't this thread's title be &quot;Wyrd Experiment?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-01-2016, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T05:19:58-07:00","id":996536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996532#post996532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;References to Wyrd become Blood Potency. References to Wyrd become Balance.&amp;quot; I presume that second Wyrd is supposed to be Clarity?<br /> <br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> <br /> Shouldn't this thread's title be &amp;quot;Wyrd Experiment?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> And yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:10:32-07:00","id":996566,"title":"","content":"Awesome! That was very unexpected and very cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:43:41-07:00","id":996584,"title":"","content":"This. Is. AWESOME! In a class on folklore I'm taking, we had a whole lecture dedicated to the similarities (and differences) between the fae and the dead, and especially between Vampires and Faeries. There's actually a lot of commonalities, and this plays right into that in a delicious way that gives them the best of both worlds while also suffering the debilitating weaknesses, plus a few extras. No getting to be a special snowflake without some pain.<br /> <br /> More importantly, extra Advanced and Epic Merits! That's always a great thing to see, especially since they're so flavourful and mechanically fun. Striking Looks (Advanced/Epic) is especially fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:38:04-07:00","id":996619,"title":"","content":"I have a changeling game coming up eventually, going to play either a deava or mekhet heritage one of these for it and get either striking looks or anonymity. And legendary striking looks has to be one of my favourite merits of all time, the image of it is just so awesome. I've got an upcoming vampire character who I bought advanced striking looks for and I've convinced my st to let me take legendary as well. Going to be a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> I love how you balanced the changeling and vampire focus so well, it doesn't feel like a vampire who is also a changeling or a changeling who is also a vampire. Balance is a fantastic integrity replacement, though with it's focus on balancing natures I'd be tempted to make it like harmony from werewolf, where 5 is perfectly balancing the natures, though coming with downsides still. Like being treated as 4 or 5 on both humanity and clarity if they are perfectly balanced. Having breaking points towards their fae and vampiric natures and maybe even a touchstone in each direction. When at 10 balance they're treated as if they were clarity 10 for all purposes but they have humanity 1 or even 0, minus the draugrhood, and having 0 balance would treat them as humanity 10 vampires but clarity 1 or 0 but again without the effects of losing complete control of the character. Or keep it as it is but have breaking points classed as vampiric or fae in nature and have a pair of conditions like &quot;fae nature&quot; and &quot;vampire nature&quot; which lasts until they restore balance (either by gaining a dot of balance or losing another dot due to acting in the nature of the other kind of being (so fae nature is resolved by losing a balance dot due to a vampiric breaking point and vice versa).<br /> <br /> Also have one more question David, why did you ban dual kith (and riddle-kith) for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:51:56-07:00","id":996629,"title":"","content":"Getting Harmony to mesh with another integrity equivalent was one of the sticking points I hit when I tried to do a Chronicles version of Abominations. <br /> <br /> I just kind of gave up because the things were supposed to be unplayable idigam-spawned monstrosities anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:21:42-07:00","id":996642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996629#post996629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting Harmony to mesh with another integrity equivalent was one of the sticking points I hit when I tried to do a Chronicles version of Abominations.<br /> <br /> I just kind of gave up because the things were supposed to be unplayable idigam-spawned monstrosities anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, Strix-Synthesis products. Equally monstrous and unplayable, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:26:55-07:00","id":996643,"title":"","content":"Auspices to Paths, linked to renown, farther away from 5 Harmony the worse your chances of Paradox, Kuruth acts as one of the Mad.<br /> <br /> But Wisdom is easy to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:41:13-07:00","id":996652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996643#post996643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspices to Paths, linked to renown, farther away from 5 Harmony the worse your chances of Paradox, Kuruth acts as one of the Mad.<br /> <br /> But Wisdom is easy to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I made a werewolf / mage I'd have them be auspiceless. Not pure, but just simply missing auspice, their gnosis taking the same place in their soul or something and their renown brands being a colour related to their path (green for acanthus, gold for obrimos, grey for mastigos, black for moros, and red for thyrsus). Being mad during a kuruth is a cool idea though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:58:13-07:00","id":996661,"title":"","content":"Given that Pangeans could use Arcarna you might be able to justify mage werewolves having totally different paths to human mages because they're actually tapping into a different source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:03:54-07:00","id":996663,"title":"","content":"Mastigos could be Snake. Obrimos Bull or Fire. Acanthus maybe Spider? I could see Time as fitting as well. River? Moros Mountain, and Thyrsus Wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-01-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:19:48-07:00","id":996670,"title":"","content":"I love everything about this. But I'm sure that surprises you absolutely zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:58:58-07:00","id":996692,"title":"","content":"I love how you can approach these from different directions, having two meshes of the same ingredients, but with totally different results (depending on whether you exchange paths for auspice or the other way around for example). I like the idea of Liches: Blood potency based Mages with a unique 'Path' of Forces and Death as Main Arcana and life as it's lesser arcana. Their fuel stats is still mana, which they can take from scourging another's Pattern (exclusively?) and they need to Balance humanity and Wisdom while trying to hide amongst mages like vampires among humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:49:44-07:00","id":996719,"title":"","content":"At the risk of being silly, why not change Blood Potency to Blood Knowledge. Apparently the Greek form of Blood Knowledge is sort of bulky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:25:00-07:00","id":996873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996619#post996619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also have one more question David, why did you ban dual kith (and riddle-kith) for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a slight limitation, since they're not quite as fae. Also, it cuts down on unintended problems. They're already pretty snowflakey, I don't want them to get too bogged down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:28:12-07:00","id":996877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996719#post996719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of being silly, why not change Blood Potency to Blood Knowledge. Apparently the Greek form of Blood Knowledge is sort of bulky.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. When I originally started writing, I was drafting their power stat as Gnosis. It totally slipped my mind that Mage used that. And so I ended up Control + F'ing it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:58:10-07:00","id":996887,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately Blood Gnosis doesn't sound right (to me at least), and still has unwanted connotations to Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-01-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:29:49-07:00","id":996900,"title":"","content":"If I might be so bold as to make a suggestion? Why not go with something like &quot;Curse?&quot; It has references to both the Kindred condition as well as overtones of destiny, a close translation of Wyrd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:44:32-07:00","id":996904,"title":"","content":"I was suggesting it for the Vampire Mages brought up by Wormwood. I haven't gotten around to reading the experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:47:46-07:00","id":996905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996900#post996900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I might be so bold as to make a suggestion? Why not go with something like &quot;Curse?&quot; It has references to both the Kindred condition as well as overtones of destiny, a close translation of Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Because I don't want it to sound negative. One of the things that always frustrated me about older crossover material, like &quot;Abominations&quot; was that even the terminology seemed to stack the deck against you and tell you that you're playing something you shouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:57:53-07:00","id":996908,"title":"","content":"I loved the text and am intent on using it, though probably with some hacking. But it was a bit confusing on my opinion.<br /> <br /> My impression is that the creature is primarily, on a rules standpoint, a vampire. And then you hacked it to add most of Changeling's characteristics. You could follow with that and make the Vampire part first, adding the Changeling's things as a &quot;second layer&quot; template, just to make things more clear.<br /> <br /> On Disciplines, I think it should ignore that list and simply assume a given clan for what it can learn without a teacher. There are some more options, but I'll need to look further to think of what I would do.<br /> <br /> Either way, it was an amazing idea, both as playing material and as the Thank You intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:58:31-07:00","id":996936,"title":"","content":"Oh, <i>my</i>. This is just too cool. Suddenly, I have an overwhelming to play an Elizabethan Changeling-Vampire chronicle that features these guys. So strange and bizarre, something out-there even by the standards of the CofD. Now I'm super excited to see how one might blend other splats together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:46:00-07:00","id":996954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996486#post996486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm calling them Legendary there because it sounded better at the time, and it's a first draft. (Realistically, I'd probably make it Epic in final draft form if I were doing that.)<br /> <br /> ...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pffffttt... Everyone knows Legendary is a step up from Epic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:15:34-07:00","id":996993,"title":"","content":"First off, hats off to you, Mr. Hill. Combining splats like this takes aplomb, and this looks excellent.<br /> <br /> I admit, I think the way psychic vampires fed in the Hurt Locker Open Dev would have been a perfect middle ground between vampire and changeling feeding, but I suppose that's nothing houseruling or a homebrewed merit couldn't take care of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:40:39-07:00","id":997021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996719#post996719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of being silly, why not change Blood Potency to Blood Knowledge. Apparently the Greek form of Blood Knowledge is sort of bulky.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty cool, actually!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:40:52-07:00","id":997022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996993#post996993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, hats off to you, Mr. Hill. Combining splats like this takes aplomb, and this looks excellent.<br /> <br /> I admit, I think the way psychic vampires fed in the Hurt Locker Open Dev would have been a perfect middle ground between vampire and changeling feeding, but I suppose that's nothing houseruling or a homebrewed merit couldn't take care of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could use the breath feeding ability that strix have for it, or use the breath-drinking discipline from mythologies. Not exactly emotion feeding, but you could refluff it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T00:46:30-07:00","id":997041,"title":"","content":"Mr. Hill,<br /> <br /> I do believe you started something beautiful here today... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:50:45-07:00","id":997083,"title":"","content":"Now I want to see what a changeling / mage or a demon / anything would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:37:22-07:00","id":997094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997083#post997083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I want to see what a changeling / mage or a demon / anything would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, going by what the Admonitoria did - perhaps a changeling who Awakened as a means to Escape, or a mage who Escaped from a Durance? They'd look like Acanthus at first glance, but where Acanthus step outside prescribed destinies to bend those of others, these guys wear and mix-match fairy tale archetypes to draw power from them. (no idea how that'd work on paper)<br /> <br /> Demon hybrids could be... let's see... A vampire Embraces a human, who was actually an angel in mortal guise or a demon in Cover. An angel or a demon using Ephemeral Cover attempts to mimic the Bargain on a dying mortal. A changeling barters away parts of her past Durance to a demon via a pact. A humanoid angel gets caught in a Firestorm and Falls into a <i>really </i>weird Extempore... And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:10:21-07:00","id":997101,"title":"","content":"I actually had a cgaracter once that was a changeling that was kidnapped by the gebtry WHILE awakening. Could be a route for mage/changeling. Id see them as more likely to get goblin vows and/or talecrafting instead of most other contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:44:49-07:00","id":997113,"title":"","content":"Vampire/Promethean. The Kindred form is already kind of an engine of transformation (Blood to Vitae), though how they'd handle being involved with the Divine <i><u>Fire</u></i>, is another question.<br /> <br /> I'd see a lot of synergy between Protean and Transmutations.<br /> <br /> Demon/Promethean (specifically, Unfleshed or Ulgan) might be another good avenue of inquiry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:55:10-07:00","id":997117,"title":"","content":"Random ideas for splat + splats while I was on the train away from books and laptop:<br /> <br /> About to awaken + stigmata - instead of your mind opening to the supernal you start to see the god machine everywhere and can see how infrastructure holds up the building blocks of existence. Mage gives partial sight, obsession, gnosis and wisdom (no nimbus), mana. Demon gives incarnation, embeds and exploits for gadget, cipher which is tied with obsession (thesis?), aether bleed out of you into your surroundings, loses oerios, and comprise causes angels to hunt you. Can learn any embed of your incarnation, but can be taught other embeds by demons. Can only get mana from obsession and scouring (scouring takes the form of working so long that your body starts to give)<br /> <br /> Making a Promethean from a werewolf's body sometimes results in a shapeshifty abomination that has its identity change in a very physical manner, starting blank and gains permanent features as it refines itself. Werewolf gives it regeneration, shape changing, auspice (which defines part of their pilgrimage), death rage becomes merged with torment except the abomination has no defined form, seeing into twilight, and can calcify their essence to regain gifts from their life. Promethean gives it alchemy powers, refinements, pilgrimage, and azoth. Disquiet is mingled with lunacy, driving people insane and not requiring a wasteland to get to high levels if he shapeshifts. Needs essence of a chosen resonance to keep a refinement or they go centimanti<br /> <br /> Beast trades soul to demon, demon takes on the beasts body but then the horror has no where to go so it goes into the demon. Normally this would result in one of the rampant, but in this case one of the demons covers is rampant with the overflowing horrors ephemera trying to seep into the cracks in the demons other cover infrastructure. This leaves the demon to try and make his covers a fortress as his quantum nature becomes a eldritch lair for the horror, resisted only by the fact that the unchained is not Kin with beasts and so the beast cannot use is normal pathways on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-02-2016, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:13:27-07:00","id":997121,"title":"","content":"The one combination I absolutely cannot see happening is sin-eater/vampire. Mood and thematics seem just too different to me.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I like the demon/beast, especially since they're not supposed to mesh well with each other ^^<br /> <br /> I like the idea of sin-eater/werewolf, though. Not willing to part with this world, the uratha accepted the bargain, but since they are part Spirit already, theyare thouroughly subsumed By The Geist- they become a whole new being, seen as a Tragic figure in uratha society for Losing Their auspice, But Also Honored For keeping On Fighting. Gaining access to Keys through their new deathly nature, they also police ghostly activities, and thanks to being able to communicate with spirits and access to gifts ideally function as the link between bound and uratha. Both krewes and packs like having them along, because of their versatility.<br /> Mechanically, there is the question of how to deal with the five forms- i considered Dropping them altogether in favour of basically turning into a Geist-form. I see Harmony and synergy as going along in a new stat similar to balance -synchronization?- rather nicely though.<br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-02-2016, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:41:44-07:00","id":997131,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything stopping a geist claiming a werewolf. The only reason they don't usually get claimed by spirits is because they can see them and would quickly put a stop to it if one tried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:45:29-07:00","id":997133,"title":"","content":"Yes, Claimed and Urged and Ridden probably happen to a lot of werewolves and wolf-blooded who don't find their way into tribes or proper werewolf society. But it wouldn't be that different from a very spiritual werewolf or one firmly attuned to a lodge or totem. It would probably be best off if the geist was interested in vengeance, which could tie into the hunt.<br /> <br /> As for a vampire sin-eater, you could either go with a vampire whose Beast is replaced by a ghost, but I'd prefer a person who was claimed by a vampiric-spirit, perhaps even a strix. Not through their synthesis, but similar to the Bargain, they offer the person powers, in exchange it does things that please the strix. The more they give in, the more power they have but the more influence the strix has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-02-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:47:53-07:00","id":997134,"title":"","content":"Some weird dread power that modifies the SP5 embodiment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:51:27-07:00","id":997136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997121#post997121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one combination I absolutely cannot see happening is sin-eater/vampire. Mood and thematics seem just too different to me.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I like the demon/beast, especially since they're not supposed to mesh well with each other ^^<br /> <br /> I like the idea of sin-eater/werewolf, though. Not willing to part with this world, the uratha accepted the bargain, but since they are part Spirit already, theyare thouroughly subsumed By The Geist- they become a whole new being, seen as a Tragic figure in uratha society for Losing Their auspice, But Also Honored For keeping On Fighting. Gaining access to Keys through their new deathly nature, they also police ghostly activities, and thanks to being able to communicate with spirits and access to gifts ideally function as the link between bound and uratha. Both krewes and packs like having them along, because of their versatility.<br /> Mechanically, there is the question of how to deal with the five forms- i considered Dropping them altogether in favour of basically turning into a Geist-form. I see Harmony and synergy as going along in a new stat similar to balance -synchronization?- rather nicely though.<br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just thinking of the monstrous implications of Regeneration <i>and</i> Damage prevention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:23:59-07:00","id":997150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=996480#post996480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. You've managed to take something that instills the most profound knee-jerk kill on sight response possible (&quot;I'm a fairy <i>and</i> a vampire!&quot; either screams of really, really wanting attention or being a heinous power-gamer) and make it instead a valid and rich concept that adds to both games it draws from. Would it be alright to attempt similar mergers between other gamelines, or would that be stepping on your toes too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I too had a knee jerk reaction to template mixing, but this is done really well. I would change the Admoritoria Embrace:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Proposed Change</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Admonitoria cannot embrace like any other vampire. When an Admonitoria attempts to embrace like another vampire, the result is a revenant, not Admonitoria nor full Vampire. The exception is if the Admonitoria embraces a mortal escaping the Gentry, while still in the Hedge. In which case, the new undead becomes Admonitoria as well. Admonitoria are capable of elevating a revenant to join their bloodline but lacks the ability to induct vampires with a clan into the bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:28:01-07:00","id":997152,"title":"","content":"Wait, wouldn't<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997150#post997150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>When an Admonitoria attempts to embrace like another vampire, the result is a revenant, not Admonitoria nor full Vampire.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>and<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997150#post997150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Admonitoria are capable of elevating a revenant to join their bloodline but lacks the ability to induct vampires with a clan into the bloodline.</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Combine to form &quot;Embracing a human to create another Admonitoria requires two humanity to be sacrificed rather than one&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:34:19-07:00","id":997154,"title":"","content":"I don't think they should be ever able to elevate a Revenant, or doing so should result in a common vampire of her sire's clan.<br /> <br /> Admonitoria, more than any other variety of vampire, should be extremely linked to their personal experience. They're literally between becoming a vampire and becoming a changelling, not being neither anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:30:40-07:00","id":997226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997154#post997154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they should be ever able to elevate a Revenant, or doing so should result in a common vampire of her sire's clan.<br /> <br /> Admonitoria, more than any other variety of vampire, should be extremely linked to their personal experience. They're literally between becoming a vampire and becoming a changelling, not being either anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what you said and retract my suggestion about uplifting revenants, so it would now look like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suggested Change</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Admonitoria cannot embrace like any other vampire. When an Admonitoria attempts to embrace like another vampire, the result is a revenant, not Admonitoria nor full Vampire. The exception is if the Admonitoria embraces a mortal escaping the Gentry, while still in the Hedge. In which case, the new undead becomes Admonitoria as well. Admonitoria are also incapable of elevating a revenant to become a full vampire or induct vampires with a clan into the bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think completely scrubbing clan from the lineage is better than having it act as a recessive trait, and agree Admonitoria should be caused by a specific constellation of circumstance.<br /> <br /> So what land of origin do you think the first Admonitoria was? Where do you think these special exceptions would be most likely to exist, and thus where would the lore concerning them be found?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997131#post997131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's anything stopping a geist claiming a werewolf. The only reason they don't usually get claimed by spirits is because they can see them and would quickly put a stop to it if one tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not so sure, Spirits can not claim werewolves and as this Stormlord quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stormlords' opinion about Sineaters</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Claimed by the dead</i> is still Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-02-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:54:11-07:00","id":997240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997226#post997226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits can not claim werewolves<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was true in first edition. Now they just add primal urge to resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:59:11-07:00","id":997244,"title":"","content":"Yeah the only safe bet is that most of the standard werewolves wouldn't like it, specifically the Storm Lords, and I'd guess the Ivory Claws and Fire-Touched, if only because a geist is not a spirit. But that's what Ghost Wolves and weird lodges are for.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> Sure the strix are supposed to have unique powers, even if you didn't want to give one Claim, it's possible one could have achieved synthesis with a geist or spirit and gone from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:20:05-07:00","id":997257,"title":"","content":"Some creatures are rare even for the standards of the supernatural, and so special that you can't find a place for them as given in the world. Admonitoria, or any other similar creatures conceived here, shouldn't have a single place were they are common, or their lore can be found. Their lore is found in the mouths of madmen, every case so unique that you never heard about. To find the simplest answers on their being, one should travel to the ends of the world and beyond. Or just wonder with the practical learning of night after night.<br /> <br /> Geist-possessed werewolves, or any other Geist-possessed Major Splat, isn't something that should be lightly thought of. Those creatures, if rare, still exist in relative good numbers and, well, dye a lot. If it was without cost, they would be naturally preferred over mortals by Geists. What the Geists could fear in those creatures, able to thwart their existences somehow without simply being prohibiting on the concept?<br /> <br /> Maybe the spirit half of a werewolf can affect the Geist in a way so extreme that most wouldn't chose that out of fear of the completely unknown?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:26:00-07:00","id":997265,"title":"","content":"Or it might just be that werewolves tend not to die in manners that geists can fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:27:24-07:00","id":997267,"title":"","content":"Remember that Strix using Synthesis on other splats is also a good source of vampire-whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:01:20-07:00","id":997292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997265#post997265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it might just be that werewolves tend not to die in manners that geists can fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can easily be assumed that way, but we need something more constructive. Something that makes it:<br /> 1- Rare;<br /> 2- Possible;<br /> 3- Unique.<br /> <br /> The hardest part is to make it both on rules and flavor something that is both more and less than the distinct parts (in this case, Uratha and Sin-Eaters), or their simple fusion (even being mostly that).<br /> <br /> Not that the answer should come from what I suggested, just that we need a starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:44:18-07:00","id":997313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997292#post997292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can easily be assumed that way, but we need something more constructive. Something that makes it:<br /> 1- Rare;<br /> 2- Possible;<br /> 3- Unique.<br /> <br /> The hardest part is to make it both on rules and flavor something that is both more and less than the distinct parts (in this case, Uratha and Sin-Eaters), or their simple fusion (even being mostly that).<br /> <br /> Not that the answer should come from what I suggested, just that we need a starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point! <br /> How about this: while dying, an uratha, low on essence and harmony, attracts a geist, offering a bargain before it realizes WHAT he is. Instead of going through with the bargain, it tries to flee. The uratha, however, Sees a chance to escape death, and with the last of it's strength, it consumes the geist, knowing Full well what this entails. The resulting surge of deathly energies burns Away his auspice, As His very core gets transformed into something else. Now he is no longer Hunter nor Wolf, but the need to Balance the Worlds is stronger than ever.<br /> Bridging two forces Policing The world, they are a force to be reckoned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:11:15-07:00","id":997331,"title":"","content":"Second edition has mostly shrugged off the 'policing the world' aspect, and I don't see how getting rid of the hunter leaves them a werewolf, as that is the primary aspect of werewolf. Also geists don't seem to care much about dealing with ghosts.<br /> <br /> Plus it's not as if werewolf doesn't have ties to Death and Ghosts in the first place. One could be tagged by Death Wolf for duty. Or Soulless Wolf if you didn't want to use Geists lighter take on the World of Darkness. They could hunt through the Underworld, a place they aren't normally welcome though have some abilities to access, at least in first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-02-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:35:22-07:00","id":997376,"title":"","content":"Also, it has been confirmed in the Geist forum that the Bargain and Claim are two independent manifestations. Sin-eaters and other bound are officially not 'Claimed'. Although werewolves may still stick to their prejudices on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:07:59-07:00","id":997395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997376#post997376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it has been confirmed in the Geist forum that the Bargain and Claim are two independent manifestations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they definitely are, as is Possession and strix synthesis, which isn't even a Manifestation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sin-eaters and other bound are officially not 'Claimed'. Although werewolves may still stick to their prejudices on that. </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember two things. One, werewolves don't have access to the books or Geist forum.<br /> <br /> A fairly longer two, Storm Lords and other werewolves don't hunt Claimed because they used the Claimed manifestation, they hunt them because they've 'intruded into a world where it does not belong.' Whether it's a Sin-Eater, a Claimed, a Hive-Claimed, a Possessed, or a Strix-host, it's something that has bonded with an unearthly inhabitant that has strange powers and is trying to exert its influence on the world. Storm Lords, as believers in personal strength, see this as a sort of inherent failing in people, but also appreciate that these things are potentially dangerous to the world around them, and thus important prey to hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-02-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:38:13-07:00","id":997408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997395#post997395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, they definitely are, as is Possession and strix synthesis, which isn't even a Manifestation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's important to remember two things. One, werewolves don't have access to the books or Geist forum.<br /> <br /> A fairly longer two, Storm Lords and other werewolves don't hunt Claimed because they used the Claimed manifestation, they hunt them because they've 'intruded into a world where it does not belong.' Whether it's a Sin-Eater, a Claimed, a Hive-Claimed, a Possessed, or a Strix-host, it's something that has bonded with an unearthly inhabitant that has strange powers and is trying to exert its influence on the world. Storm Lords, as believers in personal strength, see this as a sort of inherent failing in people, but also appreciate that these things are potentially dangerous to the world around them, and thus important prey to hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, werewolves be werewolves and they will do their hunt. My point was for the discussion about making mix splats. Those should be thought about with awareness that the Bound are not Geist-Claimed. So whether or not a werewolf can be Claimed means nothing about whether they can accept the Bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:47:08-07:00","id":997462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997313#post997313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point!<br /> How about this: while dying, an uratha, low on essence and harmony, attracts a geist, offering a bargain before it realizes WHAT he is. Instead of going through with the bargain, it tries to flee. The uratha, however, Sees a chance to escape death, and with the last of it's strength, it consumes the geist, knowing Full well what this entails. The resulting surge of deathly energies burns Away his auspice, As His very core gets transformed into something else. Now he is no longer Hunter nor Wolf, but the need to Balance the Worlds is stronger than ever.<br /> Bridging two forces Policing The world, they are a force to be reckoned with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going in the constructive method, I think we have something here we can use. The Claim Manifestation isn't in the equation, so lets get rid of it at once in this discussion.<br /> <br /> Now, I agree that World Police isn't an aspect of Werewolf anymore. Or, to be precise, it was clarified as a consequence of Territory and Hunt. But this idea already gives us a good measure of Hunt.<br /> <br /> The Geists are strange ephemeral entities, and never were as well defined as the others. It can be observed, though, that they seem to be a transition from Ghost to Spirit. And them we have the themes on werewolf, or, to be more precise, on the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Spirits are cannibals by nature, and when they consume other spirits they incorporate the essence, power and nature of the victim. This isn't a problem for them, just a part of their life. Geists, on the other hand, came from a world where violence and decay are common, but there <u>are</u> rules, and where cannibalism too frequently a taboo. They still bond with mortals in some way, and that reinforces this view on cannibalism.<br /> <br /> A werewolf, being part spirit, can draw power from cannibalism, but as part human can't lightly choose to do so with their own kind, including their human side. Consuming a Geist, another kind of human-spirit hybrid, to stave off death, seems like a powerful enough theme for me, burning the Uratha with stranger essence that is so close at the same time, and making her something new in the process, nor Werewolf, nor Bound, nor Spirit, nor Ghost, maybe not even too much matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:49:42-07:00","id":997538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997226#post997226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what land of origin do you think the first Admonitoria was? Where do you think these special exceptions would be most likely to exist, and thus where would the lore concerning them be found</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily indicative of their land of origin, but as pointed out before, slavic mythology has many examples where the undead and fairies intersected in one way or another, and the regions where those beliefs originated seem particularly rich ground for the existence of the Admonitoria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:25:32-07:00","id":997571,"title":"","content":"Many mythologies and folk tales have a great deal of crossover between fae and the undead, especially ghosts. I'd love to see a Changeling/Geist cross-template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T04:17:24-07:00","id":997627,"title":"","content":"This brings to my mind the Banshee and the Dulahan, two favorites of mine. And, actually, the distinction between all those creatures is too modern, too alien to the original source. The people who created those stories seldom had so much a notion of classification.<br /> <br /> Now, both the Hedge and the Lower Depts bring the notion of gradual change, of outsiders slowly transforming into something new and proper to the land. At some level it is hinted that maybe the two realms don't even have true natives, but the creatures that pass for natives are really outsiders who spent too much time in there.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, I think of a Ghost who takes on the role of Guardian of Crossroads, entering the Hedge where it is accessible enough to block or invite the living. On the other hand, some fae can take the role of Psychopomp, guiding the dead throw the Upper Reaches to the Lower Depts.<br /> <br /> So, this need some hammering, but what you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:02:38-07:00","id":997634,"title":"","content":"By Lower Depths I assume you mean Lower Mysteries. Lower Depths is something else altogether. I just want to point it out for others since I was quite confused until I realized what you meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-03-2016, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:11:29-07:00","id":997637,"title":"","content":"This is really cool. But it occurs to me can these Fae Vampires join Changeling Courts and Vampire Covenants? Do they have they're own organizations instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:19:24-07:00","id":997638,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of a question I had, if a Vampire using the Ziva Coils to temparily become human, get pregnate from sex with a fae incubus, is the baby a Dampyr or Cambion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:39:43-07:00","id":997643,"title":"","content":"A Dampion? Campyr?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:00:02-07:00","id":997648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997637#post997637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really cool. But it occurs to me can these Fae Vampires join Changeling Courts and Vampire Covenants? Do they have they're own organizations instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any reason they wouldn't be able to join Courts or Covenants? In fact, is there any reason why beings other than changelings and vampires wouldn't be able to join Courts or Covenants?<br /> I honestly don't know if there are any mystical requirements to Courts (haven't read enough about Changeling yet) but there's nothing stopping open minded Covenants from accepting non-vampires (other than ghouls).<br /> <br /> Humans might have a hard time joining without becoming ghouls, but having a werewolf (and their entire pack) on your side makes some of your arguments a bit more compelling while mages are walking swizz army knives with their versatility and utility.<br /> (Sidenote: A well rounded Cabal can cast Invisibility, Lodestone (to remove their own scent), Control Sound (remove their own sounds), Incognito Presence (basically Obfuscate just in case someone would perceive them despite the previous spells), Telepathy (soundless communication), Zoom In+The Outward and Inward Eye (see absolutely everything for Arcanum dot miles), Co-Location (to bail once you have everything) as well as a multitude of spells to bypass basically all security systems. This is how my Cabal managed to infiltrate a Seer Sanctum in the basement of a private security company. Vampires would LOVE to have allies that can find and infiltrate the Haven of any rival. And hate how they can't protect themselves against their &quot;allies&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul in particular would also love to invite other supers just for the chance to study them, but paradoxically they're probably the least likely to have other creatures wanting to join since they wouldn't be able to progress in ranks (and who the hell is content being called slave?).<br /> Of course it's going to be far from common (whatwith the suspicion, paranoia, lack of reasons to join, and conflicting ideas and ideals between different types of supernaturals) but it's not prohibited unless a local leader of a covenant wills it so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997638#post997638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me of a question I had, if a Vampire using the Ziva Coils to temparily become human, get pregnate from sex with a fae incubus, is the baby a Dampyr or Cambion?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notably, if a vampire is impregnated in her human flesh, the body makes due to carry through to term. But what happens to these half-damned children? </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> We don't even know what a &quot;regular&quot; human/vampire child would become so it's difficult to come up with any reasonable guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:26:04-07:00","id":997656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997637#post997637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really cool. But it occurs to me can these Fae Vampires join Changeling Courts and Vampire Covenants? Do they have they're own organizations instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no inherent prohibitions. I could, however, see some Lost Courts being a bit iffy on allowing them membership. Others, not so much. But I imagine they'd have very little trouble with most Covenants in most cities, so long as they didn't draw too much attention. I also imagine they'd want to keep extra careful not to fall under an Ordo Dracul's knife. Studying one of these things could be invaluable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:27:04-07:00","id":997658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997638#post997638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me of a question I had, if a Vampire using the Ziva Coils to temparily become human, get pregnate from sex with a fae incubus, is the baby a Dampyr or Cambion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the answer to that question is a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:03:20-07:00","id":997696,"title":"","content":"&quot;We don't even know what a &quot;regular&quot; human/vampire child would become so it's difficult to come up with any reasonable guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes we do, its a Dampyr, they're going to be in the VtR 2e book half damned along with a focus on reverants and ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:06:00-07:00","id":997699,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but we don't know anything about 2e dhampyrs apart form their name. They're probably a bit different to the Wicked Dead sort. <br /> <br /> Hell, there might be multiple types based on what mojo you used to get pregnant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:37:10-07:00","id":997742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997699#post997699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but we don't know anything about 2e dhampyrs apart form their name. They're probably a bit different to the Wicked Dead sort.<br /> <br /> Hell, there might be multiple types based on what mojo you used to get pregnant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I for one certainly hope so. The Wicked Dead sort were quite disappointing for a lot of ink spilt. &quot;OMGICAN'TEATUWTFBBQ!!!1eleventeen&quot; is, frankly, super boring for nWoD. Just take a merit &quot;unpalatable&quot; and call it a day (night?).<br /> <br /> Now, making Dampyrs function like VtM revenants (create own vitae, daily) would both fit the trope of half-vampires and make them perfect vampire hunters/masquerade problems. The Covenants would STILL have every reason under the moon to forbid the kind of experimentation that results in them, and as individuals their lives would STILL be filled with the requisite angst.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:05:00-07:00","id":997751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997133#post997133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a vampire sin-eater, you could either go with a vampire whose Beast is replaced by a ghost, but I'd prefer a person who was claimed by a vampiric-spirit, perhaps even a strix. Not through their synthesis, but similar to the Bargain, they offer the person powers, in exchange it does things that please the strix. The more they give in, the more power they have but the more influence the strix has.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very interesting idea. I'm reminded of all those VtM powers that involved sending one's beast out to do X or Y, at risk of it getting destroyed and then... you're F'ed? Anyway, it was always unclear what might happen to the vampire who's beast is lost somehow. This points that perhaps that &quot;hole&quot; might get filled by--something else! (Note: I'm note encyclopedic enough in terms of VtR powers to remember if loss-of-beast is a clear side-effect. Please forgive me.)<br /> <br /> A vampire who loses control and doesn't become a simple killing machine... but becomes simply in pursuit of an alien set of objectives, would work thematically just as well. Maybe a spirit/idigam? Maybe a particularly weak Strix (a failed possession attempt perhaps?), maybe a ghost? Plus, it gives the character a very different inner monologue. <br /> <br /> Going in a different direction for a minute: I'd still like to see the same balanced combination approach taken to a mage-&gt;vampire, as applied for the Admonitoria. We've got the Tremere reverted to their Ars Magica origins, but that leaves a big gap in the &quot;sure I have cosmic power but not going to live forever&quot; area.<br /> <br /> Something I was intending to flesh out would involve a ghoul mage who wants that &quot;lives forever&quot; part and is willing to sacrifice Swiss Army knife magic and potential ascension for it. Would involve a custom Legacy showing how to transition rotes into vitae-fueled abilities (VtR 2.0e treatment might make them tied to merits for each of the spheres), and impose a penalty on true magic based on how much older than a normal lifespan our ghoul-mage lasts. Eventually, he'll be unable to perform true magic without serious paradox, but should have a good stock of vitae-fueled, paradox-free effects on-hand (Paths, whatever).<br /> <br /> This Legacy was going to be the actual genesis for &quot;Tremere&quot; hermetic blood thaumaturgy, but that's a story to be written.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:16:32-07:00","id":997754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997751#post997751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Something I was intending to flesh out would involve a ghoul mage who wants that &quot;lives forever&quot; part and is willing to sacrifice Swiss Army knife magic and potential ascension for it. Would involve a custom Legacy showing how to transition rotes into vitae-fueled abilities (VtR 2.0e treatment might make them tied to merits for each of the spheres), and impose a penalty on true magic based on how much older than a normal lifespan our ghoul-mage lasts. Eventually, he'll be unable to perform true magic without serious paradox, but should have a good stock of vitae-fueled, paradox-free effects on-hand (Paths, whatever).<br /> <br /> This Legacy was going to be the actual genesis for &quot;Tremere&quot; hermetic blood thaumaturgy, but that's a story to be written.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Beware, this way lies Ashtray-dom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nah, seriously the only flaw there is that there are plenty of paths to immortality that <i>don't</i> require sacrificing your magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-03-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:03:13-07:00","id":997778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997754#post997754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beware, this way lies Ashtray-dom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry that this post does not contribute meaningfully to the topic, but I just wanted to say I appreciated this sentence more than you could know xD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:12:34-07:00","id":997847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997742#post997742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I for one certainly hope so. The Wicked Dead sort were quite disappointing for a lot of ink spilt. &quot;OMGICAN'TEATUWTFBBQ!!!1eleventeen&quot; is, frankly, super boring for nWoD. Just take a merit &quot;unpalatable&quot; and call it a day (night?).<br /> <br /> Now, making Dampyrs function like VtM revenants (create own vitae, daily) would both fit the trope of half-vampires and make them perfect vampire hunters/masquerade problems. The Covenants would STILL have every reason under the moon to forbid the kind of experimentation that results in them, and as individuals their lives would STILL be filled with the requisite angst.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>My take:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dhampyr Write Up</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dhampyr</b></span><br /> Some vampires perform strange experiments producing life with borrowed vitality, through ill-advised acts of passion during fits of temorary mortality, or strange curses and contract can produce a living child. These children are born with a curiosity for the supernatural and traits which make them particularly dangerous for the Kindred community.<br /> <b>Becoming a Dhampyr:</b><br /> Dhampyrs are always born with this minor template.<br /> <b>Tags Gained: </b>Vampire<br /> <b>Sanguine Will:</b> May spend Vitae instead of Willpower to use Dread Powers, and may spend Willpower instead of other Vitae when using a Discipline. This does not grant a Vitae Pool, which must be acquired from another source for this to be applicable for the character.<br /> <b>Potency: </b>The character gains one dot of Potency as if he were a Horror, this affect Willpower Capacity, and Supernatural Tolerance. For those with a Major Template the Supernatural Tolerance does stack with that granted by the splat\u2019s Power Stat.<br /> <b>Crushed by Banality: </b>Every month a dhampyr goes without fulfilling their feeding Aspiration the lose access to a Willpower Dot, but upon fulfilling the Dhampyr\u2019s Feeding Aspiration he regains access to all the Willpower Dots they lost access to, in the state they were lost in(filled with Willpower Points or empty). Dhampyrs also gain Willpower points by fulfilling their Feeding Aspiration. Unlike other types of Aspirations the Feeding Aspiration does not grant Beats.<br /> <b>Feeding Aspiration:</b> Seek out the supernatural<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b><br /> <b>Vampires Heckles</b><br /> Dhampyr has incredibly honed senses for creatures with the Vampire Tag (such as Revenants, other Dhampyres, Bloddbathers, Vampires, and Strix) and gains a +4 bonus to all Perception rolls, and applies 9-Again to the dice pool.<br /> <b>Unnatural Vitality</b><br /> Dhampyr possesses incredible powers of regeneration. As a reflexive action once per turn, the creature can spend 1 Willpower per round, healing one point of lethal damage or two points of bashing damage for each Willpower expended in this way.<br /> <b>Foul Blood</b><br /> Dhampyr's blood has a metaphysical repulsiveness to it. This inflicts the moderate version of the Sick Tilt upon any being that bites the Dhampire for lethal damage or otherwise gets the dhampyr's blood in their mouth; This happens automatically when the dhampyre is bit, or the dhampyre may take blood from an existing wound and force some into their opponent's mouth with an Control Weapon check during a grapple. A dhampyr is immune to the sickening affect their own blood, but not the blood of other dhampyrs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run Minor templates as rank 1 Horrors, as can bee seen in my home-brew. One advantage is that it allows me to write minor templates very quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-03-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:40:00-07:00","id":997916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997656#post997656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are no inherent prohibitions. I could, however, see some Lost Courts being a bit iffy on allowing them membership. Others, not so much. But I imagine they'd have very little trouble with most Covenants in most cities, so long as they didn't draw too much attention. I also imagine they'd want to keep extra careful not to fall under an Ordo Dracul's knife. Studying one of these things could be invaluable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've knowdeced that you didn't exclude entitlements as something hey can join. Was this intentional or was this because when you wrote this entitlement were not finished yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T16:39:30-07:00","id":997954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997916#post997916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've knowdeced that you didn't exclude entitlements as something hey can join. Was this intentional or was this because when you wrote this entitlement were not finished yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I didn't include them for the same reason I didn't include Covenants. They're largely social groups, so yes, they can join, but it's a word count can of worms to address.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:23:30-07:00","id":998016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997634#post997634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Lower Depths I assume you mean Lower Mysteries. Lower Depths is something else altogether. I just want to point it out for others since I was quite confused until I realized what you meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too much time since I read the books, and I'm without them by now. Sorry, and thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997637#post997637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really cool. But it occurs to me can these Fae Vampires join Changeling Courts and Vampire Covenants? Do they have they're own organizations instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever you want. I see no reason whatsoever to bound affiliation to any organization to mechanically being a given splat.<br /> <br /> So, if the character wants to join a given Covenant and/or Court, and convinces the members to be accepted, I see no reason for this not to work. Actually, in my chronicles it isn't even too rare to have a member to one organization that isn't at all a member of the usual splat. It runs completely on shared interests.<br /> <br /> That said, the ST should analyze and work any mechanical benefit of the membership actually tied to the splat at an individual level. It is impossible to address every possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997751#post997751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a very interesting idea. I'm reminded of all those VtM powers that involved sending one's beast out to do X or Y, at risk of it getting destroyed and then... you're F'ed? Anyway, it was always unclear what might happen to the vampire who's beast is lost somehow. This points that perhaps that &quot;hole&quot; might get filled by--something else! (Note: I'm note encyclopedic enough in terms of VtR powers to remember if loss-of-beast is a clear side-effect. Please forgive me.)<br /> <br /> A vampire who loses control and doesn't become a simple killing machine... but becomes simply in pursuit of an alien set of objectives, would work thematically just as well. Maybe a spirit/idigam? Maybe a particularly weak Strix (a failed possession attempt perhaps?), maybe a ghost? Plus, it gives the character a very different inner monologue.<br /> <br /> Going in a different direction for a minute: I'd still like to see the same balanced combination approach taken to a mage-&gt;vampire, as applied for the Admonitoria. We've got the Tremere reverted to their Ars Magica origins, but that leaves a big gap in the &quot;sure I have cosmic power but not going to live forever&quot; area.<br /> <br /> Something I was intending to flesh out would involve a ghoul mage who wants that &quot;lives forever&quot; part and is willing to sacrifice Swiss Army knife magic and potential ascension for it. Would involve a custom Legacy showing how to transition rotes into vitae-fueled abilities (VtR 2.0e treatment might make them tied to merits for each of the spheres), and impose a penalty on true magic based on how much older than a normal lifespan our ghoul-mage lasts. Eventually, he'll be unable to perform true magic without serious paradox, but should have a good stock of vitae-fueled, paradox-free effects on-hand (Paths, whatever).<br /> <br /> This Legacy was going to be the actual genesis for &quot;Tremere&quot; hermetic blood thaumaturgy, but that's a story to be written.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>As another baseline for this stuff, I think it should remain in the realm of &quot;the unlikely encounter of worlds&quot;, instead of any single entity being able to just take the path for the Mixed Splat. So it is too much for a Strix to simply decide to strike the Bargain as a Geist, nor a Mage should find a Legacy so able to truly make her into another Major Splat.<br /> <br /> That said, lets construct. Maybe in the Vampire-Geist, we could use <u>the Draugr</u> as a starting point? It is death to the Humanitas in the Kindred. What if a Geist, taking the leave of the last remnants of a human soul from the undead body as a true death, strikes the Bargain with said soul, giving it another take in the fight against the Beast? The result is a second chance, but not the kind the Geist expected to create, once it finds out it will not be the only thing influencing the host.<br /> <br /> Now, how could the Embrace spoil the Awakening, or the Awakening affect the Cursed? The first and most obvious, an Embrace on a mortal in the verge of Awakening, or even during the process of Awakening. On the Legacy take, I do not think of a Legacy that turns a Mage into a Vampire. But what about a Mage <b>teaching a Legacy</b> to a Vampire? What about a Vampire that braves through a incursion of the Abyss and find the way to a Supernal Realm? Maybe the Kindred, being what they are, can brace themselves against the Abyss in a way no Mage can, and find the secret and most direct ways. But how would the Curse corrupt the Supernal?<br /> <br /> <b>Elfive</b> appointed one thing we need to keep in mind, at every instant here: this is tentative and cautious so we never, ever, doesn't matter what happens, never give again raise to the Height...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:46:02-07:00","id":998058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=998016#post998016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever you want. I see no reason whatsoever to bound affiliation to any organization to mechanically being a given splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>To properly be a member of a Court you do have to be able to make pledges (which can only be done by changelings, admonitoria, and maybe gentry), so you basically would have to be a member of the splat for some organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T06:40:09-07:00","id":998203,"title":"","content":"I'd say Changelings, Fae Touched, and Admonitoria can joined Courts, most Fae can do pledges of the Sealing type, some can also do Pledges of the Bargain type, except Fetches who can't do pledges at all, but I think, but only Changeling, Fae Touched, and now Admonitoria can do the Oaths Pledges, which you need to join a Court. Courts are designed to protect Changeling from Gentry, so no, I don't think Gentry can join them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T06:44:25-07:00","id":998204,"title":"","content":"Unless the Gentry was hiding or banished for some reason. Kind of the catch phrase of the CofD, in a way. This is an absolute rule, until it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T14:26:45-07:00","id":998434,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between being a member of the group and having some mechanical effects of its customs.<br /> <br /> First, the Changeling do have ways to make Pledges with non-fae. If the candidate can't make an Oath Pledge by herself, it doesn't mean the Changelings of the Court can't create an alternative that rests solely on their connection to the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Second, the Court can simply find a compromise to consider a given individual a member for all effects, if one that can't reinforce some Pledges with the Wyrd. By the way, the individual can still <u>make</u> the pledge, just can't infuse it with power. And depending on the individual, even if not in the way Changelings do it, she actually <u>can</u> infuse it with power. Invictus' vampires and Acanthus' Mages are both examples of individuals with actual power to infuse an Oath with power in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:13:28-08:00","id":999967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QZVMB-TKTzQXJ2biFUooMWH8vpJ7orK8khx4uYKYeJA/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QZVMB-TKTzQXJ2biFUooMWH8vpJ7orK8khx4uYKYeJA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QZVMB-TKTzQXJ2biFUooMWH8vpJ7orK8khx4uYKYeJA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QZVMB-TKTzQXJ2biFUooMWH8vpJ7orK8khx4uYKYeJA/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A friends response to this, posting it for them since they lack a account. I mostly agree with it, this attempt at a crossover leaves it as vampires that have some weaknesses added to them but far, far more advantages. <br /> <br /> Also they seem to still be writing parts/adding things they missed want to addressed brought up since the original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:57:17-08:00","id":1000021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faster-Than-FedEx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=999967#post999967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QZVMB-TKTzQXJ2biFUooMWH8vpJ7orK8khx4uYKYeJA/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...x4uYKYeJA/edit</a><br /> <br /> A friends response to this, posting it for them since they lack a account. I mostly agree with it, this attempt at a crossover leaves it as vampires that have some weaknesses added to them but far, far more advantages. <br /> <br /> Also they seem to still be writing parts/adding things they missed want to addressed brought up since the original post.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">I'm going to read between the lines here a bit and assume that &quot;your friend&quot; is posting through you because they are savvy enough to know that posting something like this would lead to them getting suspended or banned. I would also hazzard a guess that they &quot;lack an account&quot; due to having previously been banned. Either way, this post is extremely disrespectful towards David, and since you posted it on their behalf, you are the one responsible for this content, which violates the forum rules, being on the forums. You are a new user, and this is a first time offense, so I'm going to make this a warning and not a suspension. But be advised, the document you linked to crosses the line between constructive criticism and shitpost, and it would normally earn you a suspension. Don't post content written by &quot;your friend&quot; here again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:58:35-08:00","id":1000081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=1000021#post1000021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:red\">I'm going to read between the lines here a bit and assume that &quot;your friend&quot; is posting through you because they are savvy enough to know that posting something like this would lead to them getting suspended or banned. I would also hazzard a guess that they &quot;lack an account&quot; due to having previously been banned. Either way, this post is extremely disrespectful towards David, and since you posted it on their behalf, you are the one responsible for this content, which violates the forum rules, being on the forums. You are a new user, and this is a first time offense, so I'm going to make this a warning and not a suspension. But be advised, the document you linked to crosses the line between constructive criticism and shitpost, and it would normally earn you a suspension. Don't post content written by &quot;your friend&quot; here again.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hi, I guess I should introduce myself. I'm said person who wrote the doc. I had forgotten I even had an account, but I checked after being linked this as the only response to my doc so far. They are a different person, I am me, I am just a mildly busy me who took more time writing while they had the mindset for it than looking up a user name and password.<br /> <br /> Now, on my doc I would like to explain myself slightly. I'm a fan of both CofD and WoD, but I'm also a person who sees the mistakes in the older material (though there is quite a bit to be praised about it), and the original pdf that Dave posted reminded me of a certain pitfall that was in WoD, namely template stacking. I've got quite a bit of experience in many games which shows that without very careful handling, something the old line didn't really have yet, template stacking doesn't work. In the end you just end up rewarding powergaming by stacking in such a way that you can completely ignore your weaknesses. Imagine for a moment if you will a Vampire who could summon full, head to toe clothing from nothing. Thats Primal crafting a suit of armor from bark or stone or plants, a simple trick for one of the Kithain but an invaluable one for a Vampire to have.<br /> <br /> When you ever want to do crossover or cross-splat creations, you have to be careful otherwise you create a situation where the incentive is with the players to power game. Now, though Dave's work was a good basis for the idea, it had problems. Yes, I may have been brutal about said problems, but that doesn't mean they aren't there. His doc created what was a splat about being both a vampire and changeling at the same time, and I liked the theme of that in fact, so I took it and ran with it while also trying to reel in the power level a bit, the idea being that you take the weakness you already have and as Kindred or one of the Lost and combine them, while also trimming some fat to make it more concise. <br /> <br /> tldr: I saw the pdf, thought there was little drawback to being one of these Admonitoria and decided I could do better, which I tried to do in a way that would give them strengths and weaknesses that fit in universe at least partially and draw on precedent of other systems. Vitriol slipped into said attempt as the line of my attempt and my criticism blurred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HoCgoLAnK2blvtrin4hFRK32LF2l4VbSZtnA6UxU84w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Chosen of the Ripple: A Jojo's Bizarre Adventure game for Chronicles of Darkness</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6916-gentlemenshadow","name":"gentlemenshadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6916_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T19:07:18-08:00","id":1000086,"title":"","content":"Noted, I'll refrain from acting like a between man in the future or at least being more careful with it. I wont defend my fellow player though, it'd be off topic anyway. <br /> <br /> But still, I do think that the Admoni should have some more negatives, maybe a social negative to dealing with either Changelings or Vampires. I mean, they're a mix of the two and as we've seen in many things, people see the part of a person that isn't similar to them rather than the part that is relateable to them. These are beings that two things at once, not a leech finger from the august court that gets along with vampires. They aren't a bloodline that had some connection with the hedge, some pet project of the a powerful acanthus or whatever. These are monsters made so twice over by being abominations of two different creatures of the dark. They're intimidating aberrations that hold powers that are so beyond the things that the 5 clans can, and have access to MORE kinds of powers than any specialized bloodline could with ease. 1-4 of contracts is still incredibly intimidating to a vampire (Or intriguing to Mekhet/Ordo) while a 'changeling' with the powers of dominate and the ability to take more damage than the majority of changelings. Just imagine being a newish changeling out with your motley, only to see your team mate take a bullet to the gun and he looks like he's just winded, as if he got punched in the gut. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:33:49-08:00","id":1000154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gentlemenshadow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=1000081#post1000081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I guess I should introduce myself. I'm said person who wrote the doc. I had forgotten I even had an account, but I checked after being linked this as the only response to my doc so far. They are a different person, I am me, I am just a mildly busy me who took more time writing while they had the mindset for it than looking up a user name and password.<br /> <br /> Now, on my doc I would like to explain myself slightly. I'm a fan of both CofD and WoD, but I'm also a person who sees the mistakes in the older material (though there is quite a bit to be praised about it), and the original pdf that Dave posted reminded me of a certain pitfall that was in WoD, namely template stacking. I've got quite a bit of experience in many games which shows that without very careful handling, something the old line didn't really have yet, template stacking doesn't work. In the end you just end up rewarding powergaming by stacking in such a way that you can completely ignore your weaknesses. Imagine for a moment if you will a Vampire who could summon full, head to toe clothing from nothing. Thats Primal crafting a suit of armor from bark or stone or plants, a simple trick for one of the Kithain but an invaluable one for a Vampire to have.<br /> <br /> When you ever want to do crossover or cross-splat creations, you have to be careful otherwise you create a situation where the incentive is with the players to power game. Now, though Dave's work was a good basis for the idea, it had problems. Yes, I may have been brutal about said problems, but that doesn't mean they aren't there. His doc created what was a splat about being both a vampire and changeling at the same time, and I liked the theme of that in fact, so I took it and ran with it while also trying to reel in the power level a bit, the idea being that you take the weakness you already have and as Kindred or one of the Lost and combine them, while also trimming some fat to make it more concise. <br /> <br /> tldr: I saw the pdf, thought there was little drawback to being one of these Admonitoria and decided I could do better, which I tried to do in a way that would give them strengths and weaknesses that fit in universe at least partially and draw on precedent of other systems. Vitriol slipped into said attempt as the line of my attempt and my criticism blurred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clearing that up! Your critiques stated in this post are all perfectly reasonable. The issue with the google doc in question was that, as mentioned in the red text, it crosses the line from constructive critique into attack against the creator as phrased there. In the future, just try to make sure you state your critiques with respect towards the creator of the work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:16:49-08:00","id":1000564,"title":"","content":"I agree with most of those critiques. I was doing my own version to better address them, but I got kind of drowned on work this week.<br /> <br /> That said, in one point I disagree. I disagree that they should take penalties on social anything. It should stick to supernatural effects.<br /> <br /> Why? Because I see nothing of this &quot;double-aberration&quot; happening as default in any of the two societies. Both are used to strangeness and unique cases among them, and maybe they don't even get aware of the true nature of the character. Or don't bother if they do.<br /> <br /> From a Kindred, the All Night Society is already plenty of snowflakes. For the more it can be distinct from a simple bloodline on a mechanical level, it isn't for the Damned. It doesn't have a reason to be. They have a number of clans that maybe aren't even truly related to begin with, and even a given member of the clan, through rules on Strix and Revenants, can actually be the first vampire of its own line, just &quot;elevated&quot; to clan status. Bloodlines add a lot to this, since any vampire can create their own, at any time, for any purpose, and most of those purposes are, in-setting perspective, not a purpose at all, but shit just happened.<br /> <br /> Kithain are shaped by their individual Durance, so they have even less rules about they. Actually, there is nothing in setting that makes it impossible for a given Changeling to be almost identical to a Kindred, not because of Embrace or Strix whatever, but just by dint of being shaped that way by the Durance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T16:44:38-08:00","id":1034940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria?p=997113#post997113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire/Promethean. The Kindred form is already kind of an engine of transformation (Blood to Vitae), though how they'd handle being involved with the Divine <i><u>Fire</u></i>, is another question.<br /> <br /> I'd see a lot of synergy between Protean and Transmutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Promethean supplements had examples of Created made by vampires, werewolves, and mages who all harnessed the Divine Fire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","dat